  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The balancing length for a cell is <math><mn>560</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> in a potentiometer experiment. When an external resistance of <math><mn>10</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> &nbsp;is connected in parallel to the cell, the balancing length changes by <math><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . If the internal resistance of the cell is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext>n</mtext><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> , where n&nbsp;is an integer then value of n&nbsp;is ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the emf of cell is <math><mi>&#949;</mi></math> internal resistance is <math><mi>&#39;</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>&#39;</mi></math> and potential gradient is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> .<br />Only cell connected:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>E</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>560</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math><br />After connecting the resistor<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>E</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math><br />From <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>560</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mi>x</mi></math><br /><math><mn>56</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>so</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ef97209d-cbc4-4f9f-b1ce-7f03036721d0-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 229px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
